{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/umachallenger"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"UmaChallenger","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"],"title":"Instance Properties"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failure is not escalation."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A configured ","type":"text"},{"code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"tex